        "agent_output": "Excellent! The bug has been fixed successfully. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe bug was on line 80 of `src/humanize/filesize.py`. The condition was checking `if value:` instead of `if gnu:`. \n\n**The Problem:**\n- When `value` was a truthy number (like 1000), the function incorrectly selected GNU-style suffixes\n- This caused `naturalsize(1000)` to return `\"1.0K\"` instead of the expected `\"1.0 kB\"`\n\n**The Fix:**\nChanged line 80 from `if value:` to `if gnu:` so that:\n- The GNU suffix is only used when the `gnu` parameter is explicitly `True`\n- Binary suffixes are used when `binary` is `True`\n- Decimal suffixes are used as the default\n\nAll 70 tests now pass successfully.\n"
